<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n22421" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γλύφω</span></b> 
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">[ῠ]</span>, fut.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γλύψω</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					LXX
					<u>Ex.</u>
					28.9
				</span></i>
			: aor.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔγλυψα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Str.
					9.2.25
				</span></i>
			:— 
				Med.
			, aor.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐγλυψάμην</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Theoc.
					<u>Ep.</u>
					8
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.806d
			</span></i>:—
				Pass.
			, aor. 1
			part.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γλυφθέν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>AP</u>
					6.229
				</span></i>
			 (<i><span class="en">
				Crin.
			</span></i>), but aor. 2
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γλυφέν [ῠ</span>] <i><span class="en">
				<u>App.Anth.</u>
				3.79
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Posidipp.
			</span></i>), <i><span class="en">
				Ps.-Callisth.
				3.22
			</span></i>, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δια-</span>) <i><span class="en">
				Ael.
				<u>VH</u>
				14.7
			</span></i>: pf.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γέγλυμμαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>AP</u>
					9.752
				</span></i>
			 (<i><span class="en">
				Ascl.
			</span></i> or Antip. Thess.), <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Smp.</u>
				216d
			</span></i>, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐγ-</span>) <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				2.106
			</span></i>, but 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐξ-έγλ-</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Eup.
					331
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>R.</u>
				616d
			</span></i>:—<i>carve, cut out with a knife</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ναῦς τ᾽ ἔγλυφεν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Nu.</u>
					879
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γ. σφρηγῖδας</span>
			<i>engrave</i> them, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				7.69
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Hp.Mi.</u>
				368c
			</span></i>; of sculptors, opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γράφω</span>,
				<i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				2.46
			</span></i>, Str.l.c.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔγλυψέν με
			σίδηρος</span>, written under a statue, <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				14.973
			</span></i>:—
				Med.
			, <i>cause to be engraved</i>, Theoc.l.c., <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
			</span></i> l.c. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>note down</i> or <i>write</i> [on waxen tablets], 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τόκους</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>AP</u>
					11.289
				</span></i>
			 (<i><span class="en">
				Pall.
			</span></i>). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			
				Pass.
			, <i>to be hatched</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἕως γλυφῆναι τὰ ὠά</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Antig.
					<u>Mir.</u>
					97
				</span></i>
			. (Cf. Lat.<i>glūbo</i> 'peel',
				<i>glūma</i> 'husk', OHG. <i>klioban</i>
			'cleave'.)</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
